 provincia de Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas.\n   - **Efecto en los datos (34 puntos con coordenadas válidas +\n   -**Anexo:**\n     -Resolución del Consejo Provincial de Esmeraldas.\n   - **Efecto en los datos:**\n     - Inicialmente, todos los dat\n<truncated 3865 bytes>\n44%), and one excluded record with coordinates (0, 0).  Implementing Option A, `MANGA DEL CURA`'s 38 valid points now correctly register as `geo_correctos`, including the one previously `MANGA DEL CURA` point.\n\nIn `EL PIEDRERO`, 68 points are validated as `CANAR - LA TRONCAL` and are now correctly `geo_correctos`. The single remaining `GUAYAS - GUAYAQUIL` record continues to be classified as `limbo_formato_correcto`.\n\n\nAnalysis confirms that an additional point within the `LAS GOLONDRINAS` polygon is now correctly classified as `geo_correctos`, bringing the total to 38,503. The remaining nine points within the `LAS GOLONDRINAS` polygon are assigned to Ibarra, despite the legal assignment of Cotacachi.\n\nThese nine points, along with the other remaining records, remain in the limbo category due to territorial disputes, coastal border locations, or typing discrepancies. With the classification changes, the `geo_correctos` category comprises 99.84% of the dataset, and the `limbo_formato_correcto` category is reduced to 0.16%.\n\n\nDiscrepancies identified include 26 records on cantonal boundaries, such as those in Las Golondrinas, where the registered canton (Ibarra) differs from the legally correct one (Cotacachi).  Further issues involve 18 records where the province name was mistakenly entered as the canton, such as instances of Guayas, El Oro, Manabi, and Pichincha. There are also 48 records that are located near the coastline.\n\nThe number of unique cantons remaining in the dataset must be re-evaluated as I confirm a remapping and analysis.  The previous count of 217 included cantons that are no longer valid.\n\n\nThe dataset's 214 validated cantons are confirmed as accurate. Initial hypothesis of needing 217 was disproven after the canton remapping. Analyzing the shapefile (`nxcantones.shp`), there are 224 total polygons. The polygons break down to three Galapagos cantons, three \"non-delimited zones,\" and 218 continental cantons. The remapping of the three \"non-delimited zones\" corrects the remaining discrepancies.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"120","Path":"\"D:\\\\Tesis\\\\tests\\\\test_reparar_coordenadas.py\"","StartLine":"1"}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
{"step_index":451,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T16:03:13Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-10T11:03:13-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-10T11:03:13-05:00\nShowing lines 1-120 of 638\n1: \"\"\"\n2: test_reparar_coordenadas.py — Tests unitarios para la Fase 4: Validación Geoespacial.\n3: \n4: Verifica que:\n5: 1. Las funciones de reconstrucción decimal produzcan cadenas con el formato\n6:    correcto para los 4 escenarios (Paso 4.9).\n7: 2. El algoritmo reparador recupera registros con coordenadas corruptas\n8:    usando coordenadas sintéticas conocidas dentro de cantones ecuatorianos.\n9: 3. La auditoría topológica (sjoin) clasifica correctamente correctos vs. a corregir.\n10: 4. El ensamblaje final preserva la integridad de los datos.\n11: \n12: Estrategia de test con coordenadas sintéticas:\n13:     Se usan cantones reales de Ecuador con coordenadas centroide conocidas,\n14:     luego se \"corrompe\" la latitud eliminando el punto decimal para simular\n15:     el error de digitación, y se verifica que el algoritmo la repare.\n16: \"\"\"\n17: import pandas as pd\n18: import pytest\n19: \n20: from src.limpieza.filtros import (\n21:     cargar_intermedio_filtrado,\n22: )\n23: from src.validacion_geo.cartografia import cargar_mapa_cantonal\n24: from src.validacion_geo.ensamblaje import ensamblar_base_final\n25: from src.validacion_geo.geometrias import (\n26:     auditar_punto_en_poligono,\n27:     crear_geodataframe_puntos,\n28:     separar_por_formato,\n29: )\n30: from src.validacion_geo.reparacion import (\n31:     _limpiar_cadena_lat,\n32:     reparar_coordenadas_corruptas,\n33:     reconstruir_escenario_1,\n34:     reconstruir_escenario_2,\n35:     reconstruir_escenario_3,\n36:     reconstruir_escenario_4,\n37:     validar_reconstruccion_sjoin,\n38: )\n39: \n40: \n41: # =========================================================================\n42: # FIXTURE: Mapa cantonal (cargado una sola vez por sesión de test)\n43: # =========================================================================\n44: # `scope=\"module\"` le indica a pytest que cargue el shapefile UNA SOLA VEZ\n45: # para todo este archivo de pruebas y reutilice el re\n<truncated 1489 bytes>\n536    | \"09592\"  → pos ecuatorial\n72: \n73: \n74: # Registros base del DataFrame de prueba (21 columnas como en el pipeline real)\n75: _COLUMNAS_SCHEMA = [\n76:     \"codigo_caso\", \"tipo_delito\", \"fecha_hecho\", \"anio_hecho\", \"mes_hecho\",\n77:     \"dia_semana\", \"hora_aproximada\", \"provincia\", \"canton\", \"zona_tipo\",\n78:     \"lugar_especifico\", \"tipo_arma\", \"motivacion_detalle\", \"causa_especifica\",\n79:     \"edad_victima\", \"sexo_victima\", \"nacionalidad_victima\",\n80:     \"latitud\", \"longitud\", \"AUX_HORA_SISTEMA\", \"AUX_MINUTO_SISTEMA\",\n81: ]\n82: \n83: \n84: # Función auxiliar (\"fábrica\") que construye un DataFrame de 1 fila con\n85: # exactamente las mismas columnas que produce `crear_geodataframe_puntos()`,\n86: # para poder inyectarlo directamente en las funciones de reparación.\n87: def _crear_df_sintetico(\n88:     canton: str,\n89:     lat_str: str,\n90:     lon_str: str,\n91:     lat_num: float,\n92:     lon_num: float,\n93: ) -> pd.DataFrame:\n94:     \"\"\"Crea un DataFrame sintético de un registro para testing.\"\"\"\n95:     # Lista con 1 diccionario adentro → DataFrame de 1 fila.\n96:     return pd.DataFrame([{\n97:         \"codigo_caso\": \"TEST-001\",\n98:         \"tipo_delito\": \"HOMICIDIO\",\n99:         \"fecha_hecho\": \"2023-01-15\",\n100:         \"anio_hecho\": 2023,\n101:         \"mes_hecho\": \"ENERO\",\n102:         \"dia_semana\": \"LUNES\",\n103:         \"hora_aproximada\": \"14\",\n104:         \"provincia\": \"TEST\",\n105:         \"canton\": canton,\n106:         \"zona_tipo\": \"URBANO\",\n107:         \"lugar_especifico\": \"VIA PUBLICA\",\n108:         \"tipo_arma\": \"FUEGO\",\n109:         \"motivacion_detalle\": \"OTRO\",\n110:         \"causa_especifica\": \"OTRO\",\n111:         \"edad_victima\": \"35\",\n112:         \"sexo_victima\": \"HOMBRE\",\n113:         \"nacionalidad_victima\": \"ECUATORIANA\",\n114:         \"latitud\": lat_str,\n115:         \"longitud\": lon_str,\n116:         \"AUX_HORA_SISTEMA\": \"14\",\n117:         \"AUX_MINUTO_SISTEMA\": \"30\",\n118:         # Campos internos del pipeline\n119:         \"latitud_original\": lat_str,\n120:         \"longitud_original\": lon_str,","truncated_fields":["content"]}
